---
import { ArrowUpRight, FileText } from "@lucide/astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import MottoBanner from "../components/MottoBanner.astro";
import flyBanner from "../assets/banners/fly.webp";
import { profile } from "../data/profile";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Tejas Kabra"
  description="I'm Tejas, a SpaceX Engineering Intern and Texas A&M electrical engineering student interested in embedded hardware, robotics, and space."
>
  <section class="page-intro shell">
    <p class="section-label">About / The person behind the boards</p>
    <h1>Hi, I’m Tejas.</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">
      An electrical engineering student at Texas A&amp;M.
      <br />
      Currently an Engineering Intern at SpaceX.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button button-primary" href="/resume/">
        <FileText size={17} /> View resume
      </a>
      <a
        class="button button-quiet"
        href={profile.linkedin}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer"
      >
        LinkedIn <ArrowUpRight size={17} />
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="about-section shell">
    <div>
      <p class="section-label">01 / The work</p>
      <h2>
        I like figuring out
        <br />
        the whole system.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="about-copy">
      <p>
        A board can look right in Altium and still give you a lot to work
        through on the bench. That’s the part of electrical engineering I like:
        getting the power, firmware, interfaces, and physical packaging to work
        together.
      </p>
      <p>
        With Texas A&amp;M Formula Electric, I’ve designed a four-layer STM32G4
        telemetry board, written its firmware, and worked through two PCB
        revisions. I’ve also built a Raspberry Pi inventory system with
        solenoid-controlled drawers and worked on custom STM32 hardware with
        RoboMasters.
      </p>
      <p>
        I’m a Craig and Galen Brown Engineering Honors student. Before SpaceX, I
        interned at Southland Industries, working on electrical design for
        modular data center cooling infrastructure.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="about-section shell">
    <div>
      <p class="section-label">02 / The direction</p>
      <h2>
        Space has been
        <br />
        the long-term pull.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="about-copy">
      <p>
        I’m interested in hardware that helps people operate in difficult
        environments. Space and medical robotics sit at the center of that for
        me. <em>Project Hail Mary</em> is part of why: I love the combination of
        engineering, improvisation, and a problem that makes you keep trying.
      </p>
      <p>
        Getting to work at SpaceX is a big step. I’m there to contribute, ask
        good questions, and learn from the engineers around me.
      </p>
      <p>
        For summer 2027, I’m looking for an internship in electrical
        engineering, embedded systems, or hardware, with plenty of time close to
        the actual design and testing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="about-haikyuu">
    <div class="shell about-section">
      <div>
        <p class="section-label">03 / A little personality</p>
        <h2>
          Yes, the banners
          <br />
          are from Haikyuu.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="about-copy">
        <p>
          I like its focus on practice, teamwork, and getting a little better
          every time you show up. The banners felt at home here.
        </p>
        <MottoBanner image={flyBanner} alt="Haikyuu: Fly" compact />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="shell about-toolkit">
    <p class="section-label">Tools I work with</p>
    <dl>
      <div>
        <dt>Hardware</dt>
        <dd>Altium, PCB layout, power regulation, analog circuits</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Embedded</dt>
        <dd>STM32, C, STM32CubeIDE, CAN, UART, I2C</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Integration</dt>
        <dd>LTspice, oscilloscopes, DMMs, soldering, Python</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
